    parser.add_argument(
        "--dart-noise",
# Privileged demo-transfer teacher: v1-based ablations

This generates training demonstrations. It is **not an evaluated student policy**:
the teacher reads live simulator plate poses, target sites, contacts and robot
kinematics that the student cannot access. It sends ordinary normalized actions;
it never writes simulator poses, physics, success rules or evaluator state.
No evaluator, dependency, fixture or integrity-manifest changes are needed.

The operator measured v1 at **27/30** on seeds 2000000–2000029. All three failures
were source slot 0; their grasps succeeded and their placement/release failed.
That is the supplied v1 measurement, not a new result from these implementation
checks, and does not demonstrate the student policy's 90% target.

## Shared replay and v1 ablation

After ordinary reset/warmup, choose the nearest demonstration by plate xy relative
to starting pelvis xy, excluding demo 45. Neither seed nor sampled source slot
selects the demonstration. `nearest_demos(..., top_n=N)` exposes the ranking.
The runner records the sampled slot only for analysis.

For demo k, the initial translation g aligns its grasp with the actual plate;
the placement translation h aligns its nominal rack with the actual target rack:

```text
g = (plate_xy - pelvis0_xy) - (demo_plate_xy - demo_pelvis0_xy)
h = target_rack_offset_xy - demo_target_rack_offset_xy
desired_pelvis_xy(t) = demo_pelvis_xy(t) + shift(t)
```

The nominal destination-rack origin is `[0.55, -0.24]`, from pinned MovePlateG1.
`shift(t)` holds g through `grasp_step + 30`, blends linearly to h through
`release_step - 40`, then holds h. Arms, grippers, height and yaw follow a single
demo clock except during the selected interventions or legacy v2 corrections/recovery.

`--mode v1` preserves the original action controller: recorded base velocity plus
2/s pelvis feedback in the observed body frame, a 1 cm pelvis gate before closing
and opening, each with a 100-step wait limit. After replay it holds the last demo
action with open grippers. There is no object feedback, wrist correction or
retreat guard in v1. Diagnostics are now collected in both modes.

## Ablation (v3)

The default is now **v1 with all five flags off**. Each flag can be enabled alone;
`--no-<flag>` explicitly disables it. Every resolved boolean is included both in
`teacher_config` and at the top level of each episode record, and is hashed into
`run_id`. The alignment audit is hashed too. Existing logs cannot be resumed with
changed code/settings; running generators already hold their previous code in memory.

| Flag | Intervention on v1 |
| --- | --- |
| `--align-then-lower` | Pause above the rack, hold that demo frame's arm/gripper targets, and align plate xy to the nearest target site's xy within **1 cm**, for at most **150 physical steps**. While waiting, use zero demo base feed-forward and P feedback with a **0.06 m/s** minimum, regardless of the minimum-speed flag. Then resume the arm/gripper clock and command **vx=vy=0 through lowering, opening and all subsequent replay**. A timeout also freezes the base and is recorded. The release pelvis gate is skipped after alignment. |
| `--tilt-correct` | Apply v2's bounded wrist correction and at most 60 correction steps at release. |
| `--guarded-retreat` | Apply v2's opening/settling and retreat monitoring/recovery. |
| `--deadzone-min-speed` | Stop the P correction within the pelvis tolerance; outside it, floor its speed at 0.06 m/s. Preserve demo base feed-forward when the clock advances. |
| `--grasp-feedback-only` | Remove base feed-forward during approach through the grasp transition; carry and later phases keep v1 feed-forward. |

All other phases retain **v1 demo base feed-forward + pelvis P tracking**.
V1's paused grasp/release gates already use zero feed-forward. DART is disabled
from the actual release transition onward in every configuration; its planar
component is additionally disabled after alignment freezes the base.

Compatibility: `--mode v1` selects the original v1 controller; bare `--mode v2`
selects the **legacy continuous object-feedback placement sequence**, with all
five preset booleans true, its original 1.5 cm pelvis tolerance and unchanged
wrist/retreat routines. Legacy v2 deliberately retains movement during lowering
so the old regression remains reproducible (apart from the requested DART fix).
It records `legacy_v2=true`. An explicit boolean override selects the independent
ablation path, retaining the other preset values; for one-change experiments,
use the default/v1 preset. All five flags on the v1 preset uses the **new**
align/freeze sequence and differs from legacy v2.

**Gate audit:** `demos_lowdim.npz` has no plate/hand trajectory channels. The
`audit_alignment.py` dataset inspection therefore replays each demo's recorded
actions and seed with CPU physics and camera observations omitted; it reads live
hand positions and collision-mesh world z bounds without injecting poses or
changing controllers, assets or rules. All **59 usable demos** have plate/rack
vertical overlap at `release_step - 40`: the plate bottom is **3.4–6.8 cm below**
the rack top. For each demo the gate is moved to the last frame within **1 cm of
peak carry hand z** (after grasp+30) with no target-rack contact and at least 5 mm
of full-mesh vertical clearance. These gates are **88–189 frames earlier** than
the old gate, with measured clearance **8.2–19.0 cm**. Shift blending finishes at
that earlier gate. Pre-action state deviation against the stored demo at the
chosen gates is at most **0.0318**. `alignment_audit.json` retains each old/new
frame, heights, clearance and data hashes; nonmatching datasets/timing settings
are rejected for the new alignment intervention. These are dataset audit results,
not v3 policy rollouts or success measurements.

Run one configuration on an exclusive-end seed range with exactly two CPU worker
processes, splitting alternate seeds into separate locked logs and merging only
after both finish. Worker logs/resume parts stay in `<OUTPUT>.parts/`; rerun the
identical command to resume. A changed seed range/options requires a new name.
Use the CPU/environment exports in “Run and resume” below, then:

